<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and eight repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 7.386 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT	 TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>	150 million    352 days   22.89 pct</p>
<p>	150 million    177 days   21.69 pct</p>
<p>	150 million     86 days   20.63 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     44 days   19.70 pct</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     41 days   19.60 pct</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     36 days   19.75 pct</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     31 days   19.73 pct</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     16 days   18.90 pct</p>
<p>	700 million	9 days   19.19 pct</p>
<p>    1.000 bln	2 days   18.90 pct</p>
<p>	236 million	1 day    18.77 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
